*---------------------------------------------------------------
* errno.krn.equ -- kernel-internal v1 process-call error
* codes (task #3, docs/SYSCALL.md ruling on ABI FRICTION item
* 4). Split out of inc/errno.equ (task #8, docs/SELFHOST-
* CONVERSION.md phase 1) -- reference-set scan shows every one
* of these codes is used ONLY inside src/kernel/*.s; no
* src/bin/*.s program references any of them (sh.s needs
* ERR_2BIG alone, which stayed narrower in
* inc/errno.spawn.equ so a userland program never has to
* PUT this whole table for one code).
*
* File-call errors are RAW ProDOS MLI error codes, passed
* through verbatim -- this file does NOT re-enumerate that
* table (ProDOS's own domain), only maux's own PROCESS-call
* codes, which the MLI has no equivalent for and which live in
* a range ($E0+) chosen to sit clear of every documented MLI
* error code (all of which are <= $5A).
*
* V6-style: a syscall returns carry SET + one of these codes in
* A on failure, carry CLEAR + a result on success (docs/
* SYSCALL.md "Return convention"). liba propagates carry+A
* untouched.
*
* `put`-only file (no code/org/dsk), same precondition
* discipline as memmap.equ -- the top-level file must `put`
* this directly.
*---------------------------------------------------------------

* -- maux PROCESS-call errors (no MLI equivalent --
* spawn/exit/wait/ -- pipe/brk). Chosen clear of the MLI's own
* $01-$5A error space. --
ERR_NOMEM         equ   $E0   ;out of memory / no free banks
                              ;(spawn image load, brk growth
                              ;past a bank's ceiling)
ERR_INVAL         equ   $E1   ;invalid argument -- bad call
                              ;number, bad fd range, malformed
                              ;parms block
ERR_NOSYS         equ   $E2   ;function not implemented --
                              ;the default for any call
                              ;number the dispatch table doesn't
                              ;cover
ERR_CHILD         equ   $E3   ;no child processes -- wait()
                              ;called by a process with none of
                              ;its own outstanding
ERR_AGAIN         equ   $E4   ;resource temporarily unavailable
                              ;-- bank exhaustion, and since
                              ;2026-08-23 fork's own verdict for
                              ;it (src/kernel/procfork.s,
                              ;docs/FORK.md), which is what
                              ;ARCHITECTURE.md ruled: "fork()
                              ;fails cleanly (EAGAIN-style)".
                              ;PRC_ALLC_BANK still reports
                              ;ERR_NOMEM for SPAWN -- an image
                              ;that will not fit is not
                              ;transient -- so fork overrides
                              ;the verdict for itself rather
                              ;than changing the shared
                              ;allocator's answer under spawn
ERR_PIPE          equ   $E5   ;broken pipe -- write() to a pipe
                              ;with no reader

ERR_SRCH          equ   $E7   ;no such process -- kill() named
                              ;an unused PCB slot or one that
                              ;is already a zombie
ERR_INTR          equ   $E8   ;interrupted syscall -- a HELD
                              ;(caught) signal arrived while the
                              ;caller was blocked; V7's EINTR.
                              ;Raised at exactly one point,
                              ;PRC_BLCK_RTRY (docs/SIGNALS.md
                              ;sec 2 "the one delivery point")
ERR_NFILE         equ   $E9   ;file table overflow -- V7's
                              ;ENFILE. The system-wide open-
                              ;file table (OFT_COUNT) is full,
                              ;or the io_buffer pool is empty
                              ;with nothing lendable in it
                              ;(src/kernel/procfd2.s
                              ;PRC_ALLC_IBF). Distinct from
                              ;ERR_AGAIN on purpose: three
                              ;misdiagnoses in one month came
                              ;from "cannot open" on a file
                              ;that exists (docs/IOBUF-
                              ;LENDING.md)
ERR_P8_UNWIRE equ  $E6   ;a file-call number ($65, $80-$81,
                              ;$C0-$D3) was dispatched to
                              ;P8_DELEGATE
                              ;(src/kernel/entry.s), which task
                              ;#11 has not yet wired to real MLI
                              ;-- distinct from every genuine
                              ;MLI error code so a caller can
                              ;never confuse "not wired yet"
                              ;with a real ProDOS failure

* -- bye slice 2 (docs/BYE.md "Slice 2 launch"): `bye
* -- PATH.SYSTEM` refusals. The file-type ($FF) and size
* -- (<= $7800) checks are NOT kernel error codes -- bye.s
* -- (src/bin/bye.s) checks both in USERLAND, via liba's own
* -- SC_GFI/SC_OPEN/LSEEK/SC_CLOSE, before ever calling SC_BYE
* -- at all (a kernel-side check cost ~130 B of procbye.s's own
* -- image against a 77 B PT_HOLD headroom -- measured, not
* -- assumed; see docs/BYE-SLICE1-NOTES.md). Only the OFT park
* -- loop is a genuine kernel operation, so only ITS refusal has
* -- a kernel error code here.
ERR_BYEPIN        equ   $EA   ;a PINNED (relatively-opened,
                              ;PRC_OFT_SETP) open-file-table
                              ;entry cannot be parked, so a
                              ;clean ProDOS open-file table
                              ;cannot be handed to the tenant --
                              ;the OFT slot index is written
                              ;back to the caller's own BYEPARM
                              ;struct (offset 3) for the message
